From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: nanokvm: declare the internal EPHY

With the bring-up moved out of U-Boot (meta-sophgo's 0004) the PHY presents
no identification at all until Linux brings it up: MII_PHYSID1/2 read as
zero, and phylib will not create a device for that. Declare it instead, with
the id the driver's own sequence writes, so the device exists from boot and
the first register access is deferred to when the interface is opened.

sophgo,ephy-reg is the whole EPHY block: the register-file alias at the base
and the reset/mux wrapper at +0x800. The mdio-mux node maps that wrapper too;
both map it non-exclusively and touch disjoint bits of it.

Must follow 0003, the last patch to touch this .dts.

Not upstream -- local to this build.
---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
index b264741..e1bbf10 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
@@ -174,3 +174,23 @@
 &mdio {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The boot loader no longer brings the EPHY up, so it presents no id and
+ * nothing can probe one: declare it here instead, with the id the driver's
+ * bring-up writes ("CVI"), so phylib creates the device without reading.
+ *
+ * sophgo,ephy-reg is the whole EPHY block -- the register-file alias at the
+ * base and the reset/mux wrapper at +0x800. The mdio-mux node above maps that
+ * wrapper too; both drivers map it non-exclusively and touch disjoint bits.
+ *
+ * The analog trim is fused per part, but the eFUSE is unreadable from Linux
+ * (its clocks are gated off as unused), so the driver falls back to the
+ * vendor's unfused defaults. If the boot loader is ever taught to publish the
+ * fused values it can add sophgo,tx-itune / tx-echo-i / tx-rterm here.
+ */
+&internal_ephy {
+	compatible = "ethernet-phy-id0043.5649",
+		     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
+	sophgo,ephy-reg = <0x03009000 0x1000>;
+};
